 2 \\cdot 4 - 291 = 4096 - 2 \\cdot 1024 + 2 \\cdot 64 - 8 - 291 = 4096 - 2048 + 128 - 8 - 291 = 1887 \\neq 0.\\]\nSo, \\(x = 4\\) is not a solution.\n\n2. Test \\(x = 3\\):\n\\[3^6 - 2 \\cdot 3^5 + 2 \\cdot 3^3 - 2 \\cdot 3 - 291 = 729 - 2 \\cdot 243 + 2 \\cdot 27 - 6 - 291 = 729 - 486 + 54 - 6 - 291 = 0.\\]\nSo, \\(x = 3\\) is a solution.\n\nTo confirm, we substitute \\(x = 3\\) back into the original equation:\n\\[3^6 - 2 \\cdot 3^5 + 2 \\cdot 3^3 - 2 \\cdot 3 + 1 = 729 - 486 + 54 - 6 + 1 = 292.\\]\nThe equation holds true, so the solution is correct.\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(x\\) is \\(\\boxed{3}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{3}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:1091"}
